cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ChemChron in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "ChemChron"
abstract: >-
  ChemChron is a program for accessory-mineral geochronology. It reduces
  LA-ICP-MS U–Th–Pb and trace-element data, calculates EPMA chemical
  Th–U–Pb ages and mineral formulae, and combines both, analysis by
  analysis, for statistics, figures and export.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Sorger"
    given-names: "Dominik"
    affiliation: "Department of Earth Sciences, University of Graz, Austria"
version: "1.2.0"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24317050
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/domsorger/ChemChron"
keywords: [geochronology, monazite, xenotime, zircon, EPMA, chemical dating, CHIME, LA-ICP-MS, U–Th–Pb]
